---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArticleCard from "../../components/ArticleCard.astro";

const articles = (await getCollection("articles"))
  .filter((article) => article.data.category === "Food Supply")
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf());
---

<BaseLayout title="Food Supply 2026 | Food Supply Crisis Report" description="Follow grain, rice, stocks, imports, exports, production forecasts and supply-chain risks shaping the global food system.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Topic Hub</p><h1>Food Supply</h1><p>Production, stocks, imports, exports and supply-chain resilience across the global food system.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Four measures that should not be confused</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>Production</h3><p>How much was harvested or is forecast to be harvested. Production estimates can be revised as weather, yields and harvest surveys change.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Stocks</h3><p>What remains in storage at a defined date. Stock numbers need a commodity, location, agency and comparison period to be useful.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Trade</h3><p>How imports and exports move supplies between regions. Export restrictions, port capacity, shipping routes and freight costs can reshape availability.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Access</h3><p>Whether food reaches shops and households at prices people can pay. Ample national supplies do not automatically protect every region or income group.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p>FAO's <a href="https://www.fao.org/worldfoodsituation/csdb" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cereal Supply and Demand Brief</a> is a starting point for international cereal output, utilization, stocks and trade. Pair it with national agriculture statistics and market information before drawing conclusions about a specific crop or country.</p>
      <p>For example, FAO's 2 October 2026 assessment forecast global cereal production at 2.979 billion tonnes for 2026—still the second-largest harvest on record—while expecting cereal trade to fall from the prior season's record. The combination illustrates why high production and logistics risk can occur at the same time.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="card-grid">
    {articles.map((article) => <ArticleCard article={article} />)}
  </div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
